.TH SHRINK 1 "2026" "Shrink" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shrink \- batch image resizer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shrink
.RI [ FILE | DIRECTORY ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B shrink
resizes any number of images to an output format, a longest edge in pixels, a
quality and a file-size ceiling. Each constraint can be switched on
independently, and moving one shows what the others would have to be to satisfy
the whole set.
.PP
Every
.I FILE
given on the command line is added to the queue when the window opens. A
.I DIRECTORY
is walked, and anything in it that is not an image is ignored. Arguments
beginning with a dash are ignored.
.PP
Nothing is written until the batch is started, and the originals are never
modified. The program opens no network connection.
.SH FILES
Settings are kept under
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/com.alpinsuite.shrink ,
or
.I ~/.local/share/com.alpinsuite.shrink
when that variable is unset.
.SH BUGS
Report them at
.UR https://github.com/alpinsuite/shrink/issues
.UE .
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://buache.systems/shrink/
.UE
